          "headline": "Bangladesh garment wage protests shut about 500 factories for a third day",
          "summary": "Thousands of garment workers in Dhaka, Savar, Ashulia and Gazipur are protesting for a minimum monthly wage of 30,000 taka ($242), up from 12,500 taka. About 500 factories have shut temporarily and police have used tear gas. The government set up a wage board on Sunday, and factory owners warn of a 'no work, no pay' rule if protests go on.",
